#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 48
#: rc.cpp:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<h1>Keyboard Layout</h1> Here you can choose your keyboard layout and model. "
"The 'model' refers to the type of keyboard that is connected to your "
"computer, while the keyboard layout defines \"which key does what\" and may "
"be different for different countries."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 60
#: rc.cpp:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available layouts:"
msgstr "Adjinçmints k' i gn a:"

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 67
#: rc.cpp:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Active layouts:"
msgstr "Adjinçmints en alaedje:"

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 74
#: rc.cpp:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keyboard &model:"
msgstr "&Modele del taprece:"

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 91
#: rc.cpp:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a keyboard model. This setting is independent of your "
"keyboard layout and refers to the \"hardware\" model, i.e. the way your "
"keyboard is manufactured. Modern keyboards that come with your computer "
"usually have two extra keys and are referred to as \"104-key\" models, which "
"is probably what you want if you do not know what kind of keyboard you "
"have.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 98
#: rc.cpp:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If more than one layout is present in this list, the KDE panel will offer a "
"docked flag. By clicking on this flag you can easily switch between layouts. "
"The first layout will be default one."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: tag string
#. i18n: file kcmlayoutwidget.ui line 105
#: rc.cpp:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

